stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> LocalNew : file created locally,<br/>no known entry yet
    [*] --> RemoteNew : diff reports<br/>action = download

    LocalNew --> Uploading : reconcile: no remote<br/>file with that name
    Uploading --> Synced : POST /api/files succeeded,<br/>known entry recorded

    RemoteNew --> Downloading : reconcile: action = download
    Downloading --> Synced : content written locally,<br/>known entry recorded

    Synced --> LocallyModified : local size/sha256<br/>differs from known entry
    Synced --> RemotelyChanged : diff: version increased<br/>(download / delete_local)

    LocallyModified --> Uploading : delete old remote copy,<br/>re-upload as new file
    RemotelyChanged --> Downloading : action = download
    RemotelyChanged --> RemoteDeleted : action = delete_local
    RemoteDeleted --> [*] : local copy removed

    Synced --> LocallyDeleted : file removed<br/>from local folder
    LocallyDeleted --> [*] : DELETE /api/files/{id},<br/>known entry dropped

    note right of LocallyModified
        No explicit Conflict state exists: if a file
        changes on both sides between two reconciles,
        whichever half of the routine runs first wins
        (last-writer-wins). This is a documented
        limitation, not a modeling omission.
    end note
